==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-nor|fr}} {{term|caillou|lang=fr}}, of uncertain origin. Compare {{etyl|pcd|-}} {{term|cailleu|lang=pcd}}, {{etyl|wa|-}} {{term|caie|lang=wa}}. Perhaps from {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|kei||stone, rock|lang=nl}} or Gaulish ''cala''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-caillou.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|lang=fr|/ka.ju/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/ka.ju/}}
* {{audio|Fr-Paris--caillou.ogg|Audio (Paris)}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m|pl=cailloux}}

# [[gravel]], small [[stone]]

====Usage notes====
Only seven words in French end with ''-ou'', have their plurals in ''-oux'' instead of ''-ous'': ''[[bijou#fr|bijou]]'', ''[[caillou#fr|caillou]]'', ''[[chou#fr|chou]]'', ''[[genou#fr|genou]]'', ''[[hibou#fr|hibou]]'', ''[[joujou#fr|joujou]]'', ''[[pou#fr|pou]]''.

